  "preamble": "Lenition of the labialized voiced velar stop [gʷ] to the labio-velar glide [w] releases the velar closure entirely and keeps only the rounded, dorsal-raised approximant. Latin shows it as the regular outcome of Proto-Italic *gʷ, so that Latin vīvus and veniō, pronounced [w] in Classical Latin, contrast with Oscan bivus and Greek βίος, where the same labiovelar became b.",
